# Examples the static backend (`jade build --backend=static`) must pass.
#
# `src/scripts/golden.sh --backend=static` builds each one with the static
# backend and compares its output to the same `<name>.expected` the default
# backend is held to. The list grows with each phase of
# design/v2-static-values.md; when it holds every example, the static backend
# becomes the only one and this file goes away.
#
# Phase 2 (core codegen): ints, floats, bools, strings, arrays, dicts, classes,
# control flow, functions, printing and integer overflow. Phase 3: exceptions,
# functions as values, map and filter, streams, and tasks. The standard
# library: math, time, bytes, fs, sh and the trust model, env, path, random
# and json.
